From 0133b98aac533a74bb8b93d2cec6ad52a10d62f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pugant <pugant@local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 18:41:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(server): concat observability + temp>0 single-drafter
 fallback [t8 stadio 2]

Spec section 4: a composed concat round mixes MTP head rows (no proposal
distribution) with DFlash noise rows (dists), so spec-dists acceptance is
impossible on the mixed segment - the server's size-guard silently degraded
every temp>0 concat round to exact accept. Add the explicit fallback BEFORE
any composition: in common_speculative_draft() a dflash-routed sequence with
temperature > 0 skips the head publish and drafts a plain draft-dflash round
(exactly the concat_off path), whose dists cover the whole draft so sample
acceptance works at temp>0. WARNING once per session (harness flag), output
unchanged.

Spec section 6 observability:
- new counter spec_route_concat_mtp_accepted_total (MTP head tokens accepted
  in composed concat rounds), emitted unconditionally at /metrics render so
  it is present at 0 from boot (T7 lesson 8b35a795f). The per-round value is
  min(n_accepted, k1') - same boundary arithmetic as the MTP impl's i_h -
  read via the new common_speculative_concat_head_size() BEFORE
  common_speculative_accept() consumes the per-seq round attribution.
- per-request slot counters printed by print_timings() next to the per-impl
  statistics: 'statistics concat: k1 = N, rounds = N, mtp_accepted = A/T'.

Tested by scripts/t8-concat-t1.sh (Task 6 section, 19 checks): guard once
per session + pure DF7 rounds at temp 0.7, metric pre-registered at 0 and
incremented with speclog corroboration, marker format and coherence, zero
delta at k1=0; full suite 60/60 plus t8-concat-t2 20/20.

Co-Authored-By: GLM by z.ai <glm@z.ai>
